# What the code graph indexes here: source code, nothing else.
#
# The graph answers structural questions — who calls what, what breaks if this
# changes, what tests cover it. Anything that contributes no such edge is
# excluded. Measured on this repo: `git ls-files` tracks 452 files, of which 75
# are Python. The rest is what follows.
#
# Syntax note: this file does NOT support gitignore negation (`!pattern`) —
# code_review_graph/incremental.py:_load_ignore_patterns appends every
# non-comment line as an exclusion. A trailing `/` matches a directory at any
# depth, matching gitignore's rule.

# Documentation, including the built MkDocs site (vendored .js/.html bundles).
docs/
*.md
*.rst

# 3D assets and simulator scene descriptions — 75 .obj + 37 .mtl meshes plus 39
# .scn scenes. Vehicle geometry and world layout the simulator loads at runtime;
# no call graph of their own.
*.obj
*.mtl
*.dae
*.stl
*.scn

# Images: 31 .png + 30 .jpg + 28 .jpeg of assets and doc screenshots.
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.gif
*.svg
*.webp

# RViz layouts — panel positions and colors.
*.rviz

# Build output and bytecode. `/build/`, `__pycache__/` and `*.pyc` are already
# in DEFAULT_IGNORE_PATTERNS; `*.so` and the colcon install/log trees are not.
install/
log/
*.so

# Harness state and tooling config, not source. Named individually rather than
# left to a `.*/` glob: measured elsewhere (claudebase
# templates/project-code-review-graphignore, 2026-08-10), that glob drops a
# nested `.omx/` but lets a root-level `.vscode/` through.
.*/
.omc/
.omp/
.omx/
.omd/
.sp/
.claude/
.github/
.vscode/
.idea/
.superpowers/
.pytest_cache/

# Captured artifacts and data.
*.npz
*.jsonl
*.diff
*.bag
*.db3
